WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.420
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.420
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.280
I'm Kurata Sana, a 1st year middle school actress!

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.160
My manager, Rei-kun!

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.950
This guy is the spitting image of a Japanese acquaintance, but he's an American, Brad!

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:46.120
I thought she was a ghost, but in fact she is Hamilton-san's only daughter, Sicil.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.920
The mysterious white bat, Babbit!

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.630
Do you know what nattosurakku is?

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:54.210
My brave-hearted but gentle ally in our New York adventures, Naozumi-kun.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.760
There she is!

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.640
It's the same color as mine, isn't it?

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.140
Naozumi... Kamura, right?

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.820
Do you want to know the real reason you were invited to New York?

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.150
Double hold-up!

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.570
Let's go back to Japan...

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:24.490
This is all wrong!
This doesn't feel right!

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.160
We will do our best on stage!

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.330
We will practice the lessons every day.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.080
Naozumi...

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:42.550
Suspense at Lunchtime

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.230
Japanese!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.770
Japanese!

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.230
I am Japanese after all!

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.030
Things will work out somehow!

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.200
It feels great to speak Japanese again! It feels great to say "umeboshi".

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.490
umeboshi=plum pickled in lots of salt. Tastes... Japanese

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.700
Japanese!

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.660
Aren't you glad to be Japanese, where even little ones can feel at ease?

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:13.580
I feel relaxed for the first time since we came to New York.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.920
Since we've arrived here many things have happened... thrill...

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.840
suspense... mystery... unexplained events.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:30.440
But who would go that far to chase us away from New York?

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:36.270
It must be one of our resourceful rivals from Japan who came after us, don't you think?

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:39.440
Brad warned me about that, but still...

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.740
You can't tell what people will do just to get a chance.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.540
It's hard to believe that they could have snuck into Hamilton-san's mansion,

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.250
spray-painted the walls and dropped the chandelier.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.370
Can't you think of anyone else?

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:57.880
But everyone looks suspicious or dangerous, and they all have something to do with our work.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.920
But no one else has a motive, right?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.550
I told you before that Sicil didn't do anything wrong!

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.100
Sana-chan?

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.890
Sana-chan?

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.020
You're not asleep, are you?

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:20.030
No... I don't know who is interfering with us, or for what reason,

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:23.650
and I was thinking about how absurd all of this is.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.240
A little while ago I was angry and all I thought about was pay back,

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.580
but now it's just a sad feeling I have.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.250
Really... it all seems so stupid.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.800
What's wrong, Naozumi-kun?

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.430
I may be the only one being targeted.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.100
There's something I haven't told you yet, Sana-chan.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:54.560
Yesterday, a stranger approached me...

00:04:54.560 --> 00:05:00.360
Do you want to know the real reason you were invited to New York?

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.910
I didn't get to hear the reason, but I am sure he was talking only about me.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:12.790
He didn't use plural. So if it's only me who is being targeted, then I can't stay here any longer.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.710
Wait! If you can't stay here then where do you plan to go?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:21.170
If you're together with me, you'll be put in danger as well! That's why I...

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.430
That must hurt.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:32.390
You're worried about what that strange man said, but we still don't know what's going on.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:35.890
Is there a reason you might be targeted?

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:42.360
Naozumi-kun, we came here to do a musical, right? We were so happy about it!

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.490
We said let's do our best together, right?

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:49.660
Things happened, but it's still our chance to do it!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:53.870
Still our chance to do it!
Doesn't that sound kinda strange?

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.580
Ooops, wrong sign! 
This is for another sequence!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.960
How should I know?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.500
Alright, I'll do it.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.010
Finally.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:08.550
But in exchange you'll have to protect me.
Even my life may be in danger!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.390
Ease up a little, Naozumi-kun.
Relax, relax!

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.930
I was speaking seriously!

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.810
Thank you. I'm glad, Naozumi-kun.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:24.980
But now that we understand each other in this matter, do your best as my partner in the play!

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:33.490
I have tickets to go back to Japan if you still need them.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.200
I told you that we're staying!

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.500
Who... could it be...?

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:47.090
Does this mean that there's someone else other than me who doesn't like Naozumi being here?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:52.600
Anyway, it's delightful to have that troublesome bunch out of the house.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.680
Geez... it won't come off.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.520
Here's some clean water, Mama.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.520
Oh, thank you.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.400
Mama? I didn't know they were related.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:07.900
This is not your doing, right, Brad?

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.860
What are you saying, Mama? Why would I do such a thing?

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:20.500
It's okay then. If you did do such a thing then we wouldn't be needed here any longer.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:27.510
<i>I thought they were going to give up easily. At least now Naozumi is out of Sicil's sight.</i>

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:32.260
Brad... Naozumi left.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.930
Sicil.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:38.060
Why did he leave? Why?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:41.480
Isn't he coming back any more? Tell me if you know!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.940
He's not coming back.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:49.490
Why?! We finally got to meet, then why?! Brad, why?!

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.860
Sicil...

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.200
Sicil...!

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:58.160
The lessons, right?

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.660
Yes, that's it.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:02.870
Putting up with Michelle-san every day.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.380
That's right.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:09.170
A little while ago we decided to do the musical whatever happens...

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:10.970
Whatever happens...

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:17.390
But reality is harsher than that, right? For example when people...

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:18.680
When people...

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:24.480
But I still wonder why it's so uncomfortable to be around Michelle-san.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.480
So the problem is Michelle-san, isn't it?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.190
Bye then, I'm going to go look for an apartment.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.110
Ah. He's leaving.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.490
Watch the tone!
What are you getting at?

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.110
Please come with us,
you're the manager after all.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:41.620
It's not that easy to find an apartment! We can't stay at the hotel forever!

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.790
Ah, Rei-kun, are those apartment listings?

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:44.670
Yes.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.540
I would like a nice expensive place.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.000
No way! We can't spend money so excessively.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.760
But an expensive place may have a little more greenery.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:54.010
The man from yesterday!

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.810
Yo!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.190
You already recognize me.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.980
You are...

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.780
Please tell me!
What's the real reason?

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:16.320
Many things happened after I met you! Who is targeting us?!

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:19.950
Hey, calm down! You think someone is targeting you?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.330
Yes.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:26.500
Please tell me what you know. All of it!

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:33.090
So that's how it is. I wanted to tell you everything I know anyway. Listen, you are...

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.130
Aaah! What's going on?!

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.760
Meddlers again!

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.180
Wait!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.600
Are you all right, Naozumi-kun? Are you injured?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:47.850
It would be a great disaster if something happened to our important acting talent!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.940
It was that man I talked about earlier!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.980
Who could the guy on the pizza-scooter be?

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.740
Ok, always stick together when I am not with you.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:59.530
When the lesson is over I will come pick you up.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:00.370
Ok.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.620
?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:08.170
?

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.670
Sicil-chan!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:12.170
I thought this was an important message!

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.970
From today on we will practice a new lesson!

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.470
We will do our best!

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:24.890
Your part is later on.
Go practice your lines outside.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:29.190
"They don't need to see us."

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.980
"Let's help them with our powers!"

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:34.190
"They don't need to see us."

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:37.070
"Let's help them with our powers!"

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.030
"They don't need to see us."

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.410
"Let's help them with our powers!"

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:45.200
We already know the lines, right?

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.000
Yes. That's all of it...

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.000
The dance after this is our main dance, right?

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.210
The "Soaring magic of love" dance.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.380
What if...

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.710
...we try it...

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.010
...a little...?

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.590
?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.810
Ah... they were watching.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.650
We did it again, I guess...

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:00.070
The water is deepening again.

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:03.360
?

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:08.450
It's a nice place, the furniture is fine, there's a doorman...

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:12.040
The only problem is the rent price.
Can we trim the price a little?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:12.960
No no...

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.000
...somehow...

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.210
...just a little bit please!

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:18.710
Follow the swing, make the price lower...

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.090
You old dirt bag!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.090
Let's see the next one!

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:26.680
Ah I see, certainly an economical solution.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:31.350
A little cold maybe,
but it looks quiet at least.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:37.440
A cheap apartment has its drawbacks as well...

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:43.570
Sicil-sama! Sicil-sama!

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.570
The roses are...

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.200
Rosy! Did you find the young lady?

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.490
She is not in the garden either!

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.000
Let's continue the search!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.290
Ok!

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:58.590
Sicil disappeared?
Gone to his place maybe?!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:09.010
{parte b}

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.980
One, two, one, two, three, four!

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.980
Folk dance is a fun dance

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.730
There is a cute girl, let's dance with her!

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.940
Folk dance is a fun dance

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.780
There is a cute girl, let's dance with her!

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:29.910
One, two, one, two, three, five!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.870
If you have a fever your face turns red

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.830
You need to rest when you have a fever.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.920
If you have a fever your face turns red

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:41.840
You need to rest when you have a fever.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.970
One, two, one, two, three, six!

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.760
Hiccups, hiccups they won't stop.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:50.800
Hiccups, already six, it doesn't stop.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.770
Hiccups, hiccups they won't stop.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:56.730
Hiccups, already six, it doesn't stop.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:00.310
You didn't sing along again, right!

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:00.310
Each verse begins with words that rhyme with four/five/six; e.g. four rhymes with "folk"

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.610
Ah, Rei-kun!

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:05.150
That pose... maybe it means he didn't find an apartment.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:11.490
I already went to two places. I told you it's not easy to find a good one!

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:15.870
I'll continue my search with full enthusiasm. I want a car!

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.960
Fight-o, Rei-kun!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:18.870
Naozumi!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.040
Yes?!

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.800
What is that...

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.590
It seems to be Sicil...

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:30.430
I made this, isn't it great?
It's a present for you, Naozumi!

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.970
Wow, Naozumi-kun, beautiful!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.100
I would like to laugh about it...

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.100
But if Sicil's here that means...

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:40.400
I made it all by myself!
It's great, isn't it?

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.150
Let's go, Naozumi!

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.270
Where are you going?

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:45.780
Listen, Naozumi!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.280
I don't know anything!

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:51.490
Isn't this kinda strange?

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.780
Why? What is strange?

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:59.290
We left Hamilton-san's house, did anyone come with you?

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.000
No.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.170
That's why it may be trouble for you to be alone with us,

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.170
so it's an uncomfortable feeling, and...

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:10.130
Anyway, Michelle-san must be worried about you.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.800
Mama wouldn't worry.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.270
Mama hates girls who can't dance.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:22.980
We're going home, Sicil.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.900
No way! Let me go, Brad!

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.190
Just come.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.990
Hey Brad, don't be so rough.

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:33.700
Don't worry, I will make sure she gets home safely.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.540
No, Brad! I told you to let me go!

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:41.210
Naozumi-kun is over there, let me go! Stupid Brad!

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.290
This week's Brad!

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:47.000
He was mean to Sicil!

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.590
Brad! Enough already! Let me go!

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:51.130
Sicil...

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:57.600
Sicil, you can't go see Naozumi-kun without telling Michelle-san first! Don't make her sad!

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.390
Why would Mama be sad? Why?

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.900
Let's go! We have to get home before Michelle-san!

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.690
I hate you! I hate you so much!

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:10.650
I hate you just the same as my mother! I hate you!

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.070
Welcome home, madam.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:16.490
I'm tired. Please bring something light to drink up to my room.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:17.870
Most certainly.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.460
Sicil! I'm coming in!

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.460
Welcome home, Mama.

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:29.590
I'm home.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:45.060
Watch, it goes like this!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.900
Their manager was a disaster looking for an apartment today.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.490
Staying at the hotel will get expensive for them in the long run.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:55.490
Just a little more,
and they'll run back to Japan.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.080
We'll do it tomorrow.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:58.990
This week's...

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.490
I hate this guy!

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:06.290
?

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:09.090
I will definitely find an apartment tomorrow!

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.510
Naozumi-kun!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:15.630
Yes?

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:18.220
What are you doing?

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:29.980
I was thinking about why I was invited to New York.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.480
Ah, the words of the pizza-guy?

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:39.490
Makes you worry, right?

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:43.410
Yes, it does.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:57.090
You will practice your lines today as well.

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.090
I thought so.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:00.300
Should we try...

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:01.810
...once...

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.600
...more?

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:04.600
?

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.090
Yo! Nice, nice!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.590
Brad!

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:41.890
I see now why they called you from Japan.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.970
You don't mean that.

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:47.480
No, it's true. I really think so.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:52.810
Let's have lunch together on the rooftop. I brought sandwiches.

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:55.780
Just what kind of attitude shift is this?

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:59.200
I just want to get along better with my foreign friends.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.860
I really hope so!

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.700
About Sicil... She went back to the mansion, right?

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.290
Yes, safely.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.580
Seems you can take care of some things.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:12.830
I guess. I am a servant of the Hamilton's after all.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:17.300
And Sicil is kinda like my little sister.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:30.480
Brad, help us!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:33.980
You're in the way!
Leave us and go back to Japan!

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:41.910
Gary?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.710
Michelle.

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:52.920
Welcome back, Dear.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:57.250
This is the musical's sound and music producer, Gary Hamilton.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:03.800
Thank you. We will certainly make this musical a big success.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:08.310
Gary!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.730
Let's hear your explanation.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:17.320
I called the mansion before I came here. What happened to the kid?

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.690
What do you mean? Why did you call?

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:26.830
You have ignored my decisions and chased away Naozumi and Sana Kurata, right?

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.700
Don't draw conclusions so hastily.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:32.500
There was nothing I could do about it. On the other hand you have...

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:35.630
Help!

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.130
Help!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:40.800
Help!

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.010
Hey, Brad, dammit!

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:45.720
